{"task_id": "Mbpp/907", "original_task_id": 907, "entry_point": "lucky_num", "prompt": "Write a function to print the first n lucky numbers.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef lucky_num(n):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to print the first n lucky numbers.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def lucky_num(n):\r\n List=range(-1,n*n+9,2)\r\n i=2\r\n while List[i:]:List=sorted(set(List)-set(List[List[i]::List[i]]));i+=1\r\n return List[1:n+1]", "tests": "assert lucky_num(10)==[1, 3, 7, 9, 13, 15, 21, 25, 31, 33] \nassert lucky_num(5)==[1, 3, 7, 9, 13]\nassert lucky_num(8)==[1, 3, 7, 9, 13, 15, 21, 25]", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/733", "original_task_id": 733, "entry_point": "find_first_occurrence", "prompt": "Write a function to find the index of the first occurrence of a given number in a sorted array.\n\nImplement this Python function. Return only the complete implementation.\ndef find_first_occurrence(A, x):\n    pass", "original_prompt": "Write a function to find the index of the first occurrence of a given number in a sorted array.", "prompt_protocol": "mbpp-function-interface-v1", "interface_source": "reference-ast-signature-only", "reference": "def find_first_occurrence(A, x):\r\n    (left, right) = (0, len(A) - 1)\r\n    result = -1\r\n    while left <= right:\r\n        mid = (left + right) // 2\r\n        if x == A[mid]:\r\n            result = mid\r\n            right = mid - 1\r\n        elif x < A[mid]:\r\n            right = mid - 1\r\n        else:\r\n            left = mid + 1\r\n    return result", "tests": "assert find_first_occurrence([2, 5, 5, 5, 6, 6, 8, 9, 9, 9], 5) == 1\nassert find_first_occurrence([2, 3, 5, 5, 6, 6, 8, 9, 9, 9], 5) == 2\nassert find_first_occurrence([2, 4, 1, 5, 6, 6, 8, 9, 9, 9], 6) == 4", "source": "google-research-datasets/mbpp", "split": "calibration", "original_split": "train", "dataset_config": "full", "revision": "4bb6404fdc6cacfda99d4ac4205087b89d32030c", "split_seed": 42, "dataset_fingerprint": null}
